hi I'm Evan Carmichael and welcome to  another edition of modeling the masters  today we're going to look at how a farm  boy whose father told him he'd never  make anything of himself use money that  his parents gave him for doing well at  school start his own little business  this is a story of ingvar calm pride  from Ikea and the top three lessons that  you can learn from his success in var  Conrad was born in a small farming  village in Switzerland where his  grandfather had killed himself with a  gun when he realized that he couldn't  pay the mortgage on their family farm  camp bride's grandmother then father  kept the business going and his father  frequently told him if you would never  make anything of himself determined to  prove his father wrong Kamprad woke up  every morning at 5:50 a.m. by removing  the off button on his alarm clock he  then focused his efforts on his  schoolwork and was going to achieve  until he made his father proud after a  particularly stellar year his father  gave him a cash reward as recognition  for a job well done  Kamprad used the money to start his own  little business a company he named IKEA  the name was a combination of calm  prides initials I K and the first  letters of the farm in the village where  he had grown up he in the a he started  off bidding for contracts supply pencils  and slowly expanded his business today  IKEA has over a hundred and twenty five  thousand employees and camp pride is the  11th wealthiest person in the world  according to Forbes magazine with an  estimated net worth of twenty three  billion dollars  by starting small and working hard  comrade was able to prove his father  wrong and make his parents proud he was  able to go from farm boy to Ultra  billionaire and become one of the  richest people in the world to take your  business up to the next level here are  three action items that you can learn  from Ingvar Kamprad  action item number one build around your  customers too many entrepreneurs think  that they have a great idea and spend  all their money and time developing it  only to find out that customers don't  want it one of the best ways to ensure  your success is to talk with potential  customers build your products and  services around their problems and give  them practical solutions that they will  pay for from the day he founded IKEA kam  pride has been dedicated to providing  good quality and well-functioning  products and low prices this has been  one of the key driving forces behind my  Kia's international success and the  company hires its own designers many of  whom have gone on to win design awards  over the years according to comp rod to  design a desk which may cost one  thousand dollars is easy for a furniture  designer but to design a functional and  good desk which shall cost fifty dollars  can only be done by the very best we  have decided once and for all to side  with the many what is good for our  customers is also in the long run good  for us  action item number to lead by example if  you're building your business beyond  yourself then you'll have to think about  your leadership style and how you're  going to inspire those working for you  to give their very best every day  Conrad believes the best way to  encourage hard work and a strong  character and others was to exemplify  that in his own life even though he's  worth billions of dollars he still  drives 13-year old Volvo often takes  public transportation in Switzerland  doesn't have his own private office and  regularly flies economy class and  traveling out of town  according to comp rod I'm a bit tight  with money but so what I look at the  money I'm about to spend on myself and  ask myself if IKEA customers can afford  it  I could regularly travel first-class but  having money in abundance doesn't seem  like a good reason to waste it if there  is such a thing as good leadership it is  to give a good example I have to do so  for all the IKEA employees action item  number three never waste your time you  only have so many hours in a day to get  work done and to accomplish your goals  don't waste them every little step that  you take to build your business will add  up the big movements forward but you  have to put the time in to turn your  vision into reality  Conrad's frugality is matched only by  his desire to never waste his time to  that end he built the IKEA corporate  philosophy around fishin C and hard work  IKEA has always kept few layers of  Management practically eliminated titles  and privileges and has almost no suits  and ties in the office according to calm  pride time is your most important  resource you can do so much in 10  minutes 10 minutes once gone are gone  for good  ten minutes and not just one six of your  hourly pay ten minutes our piece of  yourself divide your life in the ten  minute units and sacrifice as few of  them as possible in meaningless activity  so remember build around your customers  lead by example and never waste your  time I wanted to end the video today by  sharing one of my favorite true stories  about embark on pride and some of his  best quotes Kamprad had always been a  fan of turning mistakes into  opportunities in 1956 a new IKEA  employee had been standing with a  colleague trying to figure out how to  get a bulky wooden table into the back  of his car  finally against company policy he said  oh god then let's pull off the legs and  put them underneath it was with that  simple idea that IKEA would reorient  itself towards the flat design  production for which it has become  famous today  you  thank you for joining me for another  edition of modeling the masters if you  enjoyed please give it a thumbs up below  I'd also love to hear your thoughts if  you want to leave a comment and stay  tuned to the next episode  you
 

